<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">State of Palestine</h1><p class="st-meta">1988 CE – present · capital Ramallah</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The State of Palestine, declared by the PLO in 1988 and recognised by most of the world, governing parts of the West Bank and Gaza under Israeli occupation.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine-liberation-organization">Palestine Liberation Organization</a>, founded in 1964 and led from 1969 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yasser-arafat">Yasser Arafat</a>, came to embody Palestinian nationhood after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nakba">Nakba</a> of 1948 had scattered much of the Arab population of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mandatory-palestine">Mandatory Palestine</a>. On 15 November 1988 the PLO declared the State of Palestine in Algiers, claiming the West Bank, Gaza and East Jerusalem, territories held by Israel since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/six-day-war">Six-Day War</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo-accords">Oslo Accords</a> of 1993-1995 created a Palestinian Authority with limited self-rule, seated in Ramallah while the proclaimed capital, East Jerusalem, remained under Israeli control. Arafat led the Authority until his death in 2004; after elections in 2006 and fighting in 2007 the West Bank and Gaza fell under rival Palestinian administrations, and settlement growth, checkpoints and recurring wars in Gaza shaped daily life.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Palestine joined UNESCO in 2011 and was recognised as a non-member observer state by the United Nations General Assembly in 2012; about three quarters of the world's states recognise it. Statehood on the ground - borders, capital, refugees and an end to occupation - remains the unresolved heart of the Israeli-Palestinian conflict.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="republic, 1988 CE – present"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 38 L50 20 L80 38 Z"/><path d="M24 42 H76 M24 80 H76"/><path d="M30 44 V78 M43 44 V78 M57 44 V78 M70 44 V78"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">republic</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:99.26%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1988 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ramallah</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Presidents of the State of Palestine</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (majority), Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/palestine">Palestine</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Palestine, Dawlat Filastin</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=2007&amp;focus=state-of-palestine" aria-label="State of Palestine on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5587 1017 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where State of Palestine lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5907 1273L5908 1277"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5908 1277h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5907 1273h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5907 1273h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=2007&amp;focus=state-of-palestine">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
